    "description": "Ace-to-five lowball. Aces play low; straights and flushes do NOT count against a low hand, so the nut low is the wheel 5-4-3-2-A. THE NORMATIVE RULE IS THE CANONICAL ONE: compare two lows by their highest card first, then the next highest, and so on; the hand that runs out lower wins. 'canonical_position' is that rule applied to all 1287 unpaired rank-sets, 1 being the nut low. 'original_ordinal' is what the source assigns, recorded as evidence only -- see ladder-divergence and spec decision SD-02. A rebuild must reproduce canonical_position, NOT original_ordinal.",
